%[text] %[text:anchor:T_8C74E35B] # Numerical Integration
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_3938052C] ## Scripts
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_AFE10FFE] ### [**TrapezoidRule.m**](file:Scripts/TrapezoidRule.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,424],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Approximate the area under a curve with a trapezoid with vertices (0,a), (a,f(a)), (b,f(b)), and (0,b)](text:image:9fb7) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Explain numerical quadrature and its relationship to the definite integral</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Describe how the trapezoid rule is derived</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Illustrate the trapezoid rule graphically</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Compare and contrast integration of a continuous function with integration of tabulated data</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Implement the trapezoid rule in MATLAB</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_82A6E1E6] ### [**SimpsonsRules.m**](file:Scripts/SimpsonsRules.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,424],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Approximate the area under a curve with fitted polynomials](text:image:9d32) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Describe how Lagrange interpolating polynomials can be used to derive integration rules</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Illustrate Simpson’s 1/3 rule graphically</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Explain the steps required to implement Simpson’s 1/3 rule</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Compare the accuracy and limitations of Simpson’s 1/3 rule to those of Simpson’s 3/8 rule</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Implement Simpson’s 3/8 rule in MATLAB</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
